# Remote inference migration boundary

QVAC 0.19 removed the SDK's DHT delegation APIs. Do not use `delegate` in `loadModel`, `cancel` or `heartbeat`, or generate `startQVACProvider`. Older 0.15 examples do not apply to 0.21.

For the supported desktop preview, run `@qvac/inference` locally in its Bare worker. The project’s deferred Node capability pack exposes its own RPC completion protocol; that requires pairing/trust, bounded requests, provider lifecycle and separate real-model acceptance. It is not a built-in QVAC delegation call.

QVAC 0.21 can expose native llama.cpp RPC for distributed GPU inference. Its endpoint/discovery and non-loopback opt-in rules differ from the removed SDK feature. Use current official examples and validate network exposure/resource bounds before adding it. It is outside the default preview.

See [QVAC migration notes](https://github.com/tetherto/qvac/releases/tag/sdk-v0.19.0) and the QVAC module reference for current runtime APIs.
